# Telescope (GAME-TELESCOPE): the eight planets, one sentence per reading level.
telescope-title = Stars and planets
telescope-close = Close telescope
telescope-hint = Tap a planet!
telescope-kind-rocky = Rocky planet
telescope-kind-gas = Gas giant
telescope-kind-ice = Ice giant

telescope-mercury-name = Mercury
telescope-mercury-kiga = Mercury is tiny.
telescope-mercury-klasse1 = Mercury is the smallest planet. It is nearest the Sun.
telescope-mercury-klasse2 = Mercury is the smallest planet and the closest to the Sun. A year there lasts only 88 days. It has craters like our Moon.
telescope-mercury-klasse3 = Mercury is the smallest planet, about 4,900 kilometres across, and the closest to the Sun. It has hardly any air and many craters. By day it is scorching hot, at night icy cold. A year lasts only 88 Earth days.

telescope-venus-name = Venus
telescope-venus-kiga = Venus is very hot.
telescope-venus-klasse1 = Venus is very hot. It has thick clouds.
telescope-venus-klasse2 = Venus is wrapped in thick clouds and is the hottest planet. In the sky it shines as a bright evening star. It spins backwards.
telescope-venus-klasse3 = Venus is wrapped in a thick blanket of acid clouds. At about 460 degrees it is the hottest planet, even hotter than Mercury. From Earth you see it as a bright morning or evening star. It spins backwards.

telescope-earth-name = Earth
telescope-earth-kiga = Earth is our home.
telescope-earth-klasse1 = Earth is our home. It has much water.
telescope-earth-klasse2 = Earth is the only planet where we know of life. From space it looks blue because there is so much water. It has one Moon.
telescope-earth-klasse3 = Earth is the third planet and the only one where we know of life. More than two thirds of its surface is covered by water. Its air protects us, and our Moon circles it in about 27 days.

telescope-mars-name = Mars
telescope-mars-kiga = Mars is red.
telescope-mars-klasse1 = Mars is red. Its dust is rusty.
telescope-mars-klasse2 = Mars is also called the red planet. It is red because its dust is rusty. The tallest volcano in the Solar System stands there.
telescope-mars-klasse3 = Mars is a rocky planet called the red planet because its dust contains iron that rusts. It has two small moons and Olympus Mons, the tallest volcano in the Solar System. Robot rovers explore it.

telescope-jupiter-name = Jupiter
telescope-jupiter-kiga = Jupiter is huge.
telescope-jupiter-klasse1 = Jupiter is the biggest planet. It has a storm.
telescope-jupiter-klasse2 = Jupiter is the biggest planet. Its Great Red Spot is a giant storm. It has more than 90 moons.
telescope-jupiter-klasse3 = Jupiter is a gas giant and the biggest planet: more than 1,000 Earths would fit inside. Its Great Red Spot is a storm that has raged for hundreds of years. It has more than 90 moons.

telescope-saturn-name = Saturn
telescope-saturn-kiga = Saturn has a ring.
telescope-saturn-klasse1 = Saturn has a ring. The ring is ice.
telescope-saturn-klasse2 = Saturn is a gas giant. You can recognise it by its ring, which is made of countless pieces of ice and rock. It is so light that it would float on water.
telescope-saturn-klasse3 = Saturn is a gas giant and easy to recognise by its ring. The ring is made of countless pieces of ice and rock, from tiny grains to chunks as big as a house. Saturn is so light that it would float in a giant ocean.

telescope-uranus-name = Uranus
telescope-uranus-kiga = Uranus is light blue.
telescope-uranus-klasse1 = Uranus is light blue. It lies on its side.
telescope-uranus-klasse2 = Uranus is an ice giant and looks pale blue. It rolls around the Sun lying on its side. It also has thin rings.
telescope-uranus-klasse3 = Uranus is an ice giant and glows pale blue-green. Its axis is tilted so far that it rolls around the Sun lying on its side. It has thin dark rings, and a year there lasts 84 Earth years.

telescope-neptune-name = Neptune
telescope-neptune-kiga = Neptune is deep blue.
telescope-neptune-klasse1 = Neptune is deep blue. It is farthest away.
telescope-neptune-klasse2 = Neptune is an ice giant and the planet farthest away. It is deep blue and has very strong winds. A year there lasts 165 Earth years.
telescope-neptune-klasse3 = Neptune is an ice giant and the planet farthest from the Sun. It is deep blue, and the fastest winds in the Solar System blow there. A Neptune year lasts about 165 Earth years.
